# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is baked into the image
# and travels wherever the image goes.

# Secrets. `.env` holds the JWT signing key, the Atlas password and the key that decrypts
# guest identity documents. In the image they would sit in a layer readable by anyone who
# can pull it, and they would silently override the environment variables the platform
# injects — so a deployment would run on development keys without saying so.
.env
.env.*

# The local JSON store. Copying it ships one property's real guests, folios and ID
# numbers into every image built from this directory, and a container starting with a
# `db.json` already present would serve that data as though it were its own.
db.json
db_*.json

# Never useful in the image, and cache directories in particular can carry stale bytecode
# that shadows the source next to it.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Tests and their fixtures are not run in the image; leaving them out keeps it smaller and
# keeps test-only fixtures off a production filesystem.
tests/

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
